Hi! I had the same problem and was not able to solve it completely.  
The error
java.lang.InternalError: Can't start the AWT because Java was started  
on the first thread.  Make sure StartOnFirstThread is not specified in  
your application's Info.plist or on the command line
occurs because Mac OS X Leopard requires AWT to run in the first  
thread. A possible way to solve this is to run the AWT headless (you  
can give the option to run AWT headless to the JVM). Running awt  
headless solves this problem but if you need the AWT, you will  
probably get an java.awt.HeadlessException. The option "--enable- 
threads" in rJava might help but that does not seem to work in rJava  
0.5.-x (I get errors during installation when setting this flag):

init.c:173: error: static declaration of ‘init_rJava’ follows non- 
static declaration
init.c:148: error: previous implicit declaration of ‘init_rJava’ was  
here
init.c: In function ‘RinitJVM’:
init.c:276: warning: passing argument 4 of ‘pthread_create’ discards  
qualifiers from pointer target type
make: *** [init.o] Error 1
chmod: /Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/library/rJava/libs/ 
i386/*: No such file or directory
ERROR: compilation failed for package 'rJava'

Does anyone have better ideas to solve the problem?

Thanks,
Robin Nunkesser

